README

Gavin Dennis
CS 4280
Project 0 

Resources and documentation can be found in each .cpp file in the 'src' directory.

How to compile:
    1. make sure you are in the Project-0 directory
    2. in the terminal, run the "make" command to compile the programs
    3. Optionally, run the following commands to execute the program with the following
       test cases:
	* make test1 - runs P0 with tests/P0_test1 as argument
	* make test2 - runs P0 with tests/P0_test2 as argument
	* make test3 - runs P0 with tests/P0_test3 as argument
	* make test4 - runs P0 with tests/P0_test4 as argument
	* make testGavin - runs P0 with tests/P0_testGavin as argument
    4. the finished executuble 'P0' can be found in the 'build' directory (Project-0/build)
    5. the tree traversals can be found in the same directory as the tests that are used
       as an argument. For instance, the traversals for the test cases can be found in 
       ./tests/.  If reading from stdin, it will be in the user directory.
